1296:Density proof (RULINGS Q34a): marker line, then every following line that is blank, more indented than the marker, or starts with ), ] or } at the marker's indentation; trailing blank lines dropped; lines joined with \n plus a final \n; sha256 of the UTF-8 bytes.
1311:when any comparative or promotion claim is admitted, including one from a screening (P-SCREEN) receipt, the evaluator checks: GATE-POSITION for the composition's source (allocator proven dense, or the four falsifiers closed); composition identity (VA14: four assignments, replication edges, watermarks); and, where the claim depends on domain outputs, GATE-W0. A claim with a failed or pending prerequisite is a diagnostic, never a qualified winner (RULINGS Q34d).
1314:G7.position.coordinates selection (RULINGS Q32e, Q34a): dense compositions need PO-LEXICOGRAPHIC-ORDER, PO-ORACLE-DENSE-ORDINALS, PO-NESTED-CUTS-DENSE; non-dense ones also need FX-NESTED-CUTS, FX-ABORT-GAP, FX-CRASH-APPEND-RESOLUTION, FX-RESUME-AT-ABORT-GAP, PO-ABORTED-LISTED; a composition not proven dense by its allocator source is treated as non-dense. A0 controls: A0-XTDB (xtdb: today's scope-counter allocator, on the A0 allowlist); A0-QLEVER (qlever: today's scope-counter allocator, on the A0 allowlist).
