1523:- Statement: Every case of CS-TYPES8-NEG is rejected with its pinned error (E-INVALID-VALUE or E-UNSUPPORTED-VALUE); the committed position is unchanged, no receipt or claim exists, and no partial row or triple is visible through any access path.
1923:- Statement: Every C6-* case: direct match and Datalog queries over :_tx/change and :_tx/changed-entity, transactions(), transactionsForEntity and transactionByCommand return O-REPLAY's outputs per JOURNAL_RULES: creation order (JN-ORDER), staged facts visible to later operations of the same command (JN-STAGED), bit-exact -0.0 change values (JN-NEGZERO, RULINGS Q21 AMB-04, provisional, flagged for Sam) and the documented and testkit-pinned fields (JN-FIELDS); whole-journal byte identity of a physically slimmed journal is checked against a separate T0-capture baseline (C6-SLIM-BYTE-IDENTICAL), modulo erasure: both sides replace erased values with their markers first (ER-JOURNAL-MODULO, RULINGS Q31f).
1982:- Statement: Per-subject atomic, idempotent commit with lost-ACK resolution. Each engine declares a route for this requirement, NATIVE or WORKAROUND (with its design id and a plain statement of what the engine cannot do natively); the requirement's own CS-REQ tests pass on that route. An open requirement never removes an engine from comparison. Starting points: XTDB: native transactions, ASSERT for CAS, claims table; QLever: log of record plus broker (PLAN C2, C3).
2000:**`REQ.outbox-atomic`: Requirement: Atomic path to the outbox and work items.**
2001:- Statement: Atomic path to the outbox and work items. Each engine declares a route for this requirement, NATIVE or WORKAROUND (with its design id and a plain statement of what the engine cannot do natively); the requirement's own CS-REQ tests pass on that route. An open requirement never removes an engine from comparison. Starting points: XTDB: tables in the same transaction; QLever: records in the same log frame.
2003:- Cases: CS-REQ (outbox-atomic, TO-AUTHOR).
2019:- Statement: Per COMPOSITION ackOwnership (RULINGS Q31e, replacing Q28's ACK clause): the source of truth sends every ACK after its own publication (CO-ACK-AFTER-SOURCE-PUBLICATION, OBS-ACK-ORDER); the pull at the returned position is served by an index eligible for it, else by the fallback, so read-your-own-write is exact (CO-RYOW-ROUTED); during a current-index outage commits and ACKs continue and pulls fall back (CO-OUTAGE-ACKS-CONTINUE), and the index catches up from the feed through a bounded queue (CO-CATCHUP-BOUNDED-QUEUE). Per COMPOSITION fallbackEquivalence (RULINGS Q34b), this holds on every serving surface the composition claims in the lane's language, native included (CO-RYOW-PER-SURFACE); a stale fallback is rejected (CO-STALE-FALLBACK-REJECTED); a cross-language fallback recipe is bound to the same semantic query identity (parameters, basis, meaning) and the same oracle answer (CO-CROSS-LANGUAGE-RECIPE-IDENTITY), with total request latency and language attribution recorded.
2029:- Statement: Per POSITION: a position is (stream, epoch, offset, ordinal), ordered lexicographically and not necessarily dense (PO-LEXICOGRAPHIC-ORDER); several Triplex transacts in one engine transaction take consecutive ordinals at one offset, assigned atomically with their assertions and the subject compare-and-set; a watermark is a fully resolved prefix and every aborted offset is listed in the feed's resolution stream (PO-ABORTED-LISTED); O-REPLAY sorts by coordinate and assigns its own dense ordinals for cuts (PO-ORACLE-DENSE-ORDINALS). The required selection depends on the composition (position_selection, RULINGS Q32e, Q34a): a composition whose allocator source hashes equal A0_ALLOCATOR_ALLOWLIST (the A0 controls) closes with the nested-cut cases PO-NESTED-CUTS-DENSE, PO-LEXICOGRAPHIC-ORDER and PO-ORACLE-DENSE-ORDINALS; a non-dense one also needs the four falsifiers FX-NESTED-CUTS, FX-ABORT-GAP, FX-CRASH-APPEND-RESOLUTION and FX-RESUME-AT-ABORT-GAP before any comparative claim (GATE-POSITION).
2031:- Cases: CS-POSITION (PO-LEXICOGRAPHIC-ORDER, PO-ORACLE-DENSE-ORDINALS, PO-NESTED-CUTS-DENSE, TO-AUTHOR).
2033:- Closure: CR-PASS-ALL + CR-FAULT; modes current, reopen, engine-restart; thresholds T-FAULT-REPS; params {"conditionalSelection": {"rule": "position_selection(composition) is authoritative: the static selection is the dense nested-cut cases; when density_proven(composition) is false the evaluator adds nonDenseAdds (RULINGS Q34a)", "nonDenseAdds": ["FX-NESTED-CUTS", "FX-ABORT-GAP", "FX-CRASH-APPEND-RESOLUTION", "FX-RESUME-AT-ABORT-GAP", "PO-ABORTED-LISTED"]}, "gates": ["GATE-ORACLE-PIN"]}.
2195:- Statement: Every repository and native helper answer row that claims a fact names its supporting assertion ids and transactions, equal to O-REPLAY's supports.
2356:- Statement: Every CURSOR_TRANSITIONS.mustContinue case continues with O-REPLAY's rows at the cursor's basis; errors occur only in the permittedErrors cases, each with its pinned error; CE-FENCED also continues after recovery.

