lab/acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md:337:**Decimal order key TDK1 (RULINGS Q35).** channel: decimal_order_v1. source: lab/research/R20-order-preserving-decimal-encodings.md section 6; RULINGS Q35a. summary: value-determined, order-preserving (TDK1): zero o; positive p LL I F (LL two-digit integer-digit count, I without leading zeros, F without trailing zeros); negative n (99-L) comp(I) comp(F) z with comp(d) = 9 - d. alphabet: 0123456789nopz. inputGrammar: -?(0|[1-9][0-9]*)(\.[0-9]+)?; refused: +1, 01, 1., .5, 1e3, whitespace, non-ASCII digits, negative zero in any spelling. decode: parse strictly, then render the sign, I or 0, and when s > 0 a '.' followed by F right-padded with zeros to s digits. order: codepoint order of keys equals numeric order; the alphabet [0-9nopz] makes ICU order equal codepoint order on QLever and byte order on XTDB (no collation on 2.2.0). useConstraints: keys are never concatenated into a composite string and never used for prefix queries (p0212 is a prefix of p02125); only whole-key equality and ordered comparison, as a separate sort column (RULINGS Q35d). versioning: a future encoding gets a new channel name and a migration (RULINGS Q35c). limits: maximum precision 38 (TDK1 has headroom to 99 integer digits); no native XTDB DECIMAL lane: one verification path (RULINGS Q35e). kernelNote: if the kernel uses decimal.js or big.js, rounding tests cover their signed zero (RULINGS Q35e).
