   259	### 6.1 Date functions
   260	
   261	| Function | Definition |
   262	| --- | --- |
   263	| `startOf(d)` | the instant `d + "T00:00:00.000000Z"` |
   264	| `addDays(d, n)` | the date n calendar days after d (n may be negative or zero), proleptic Gregorian |
   265	| `endOfDay(d)` | `startOf(addDays(d, 1))`: "due by the end of day d" means due at the next midnight UTC |
   266	| `dateOf(t)` | the first 10 characters of instant t |
   267	| `weekday(d)` | ISO weekday of d, 1 = Monday to 7 = Sunday |
   268	| `addBusinessDays(d, n)`, n >= 1 | step forward one calendar day at a time from d, counting each day whose weekday is 1 to 5, and return the day on which the count reaches n. d itself is never counted. There are no holidays. |
   269	
   270	Examples: `addBusinessDays(2026-11-02 Mon, 3) = 2026-11-05 Thu`; `addBusinessDays(2026-11-06 Fri, 3) = 2026-11-11 Wed`;
