  1093	Role: measurement size for P1 to P5 and the golden scenarios; not a target in itself (lab/SCOPE.md section 2 item 2). Source: lab/TARGETS.md section 2 (year-one scale; rungs 10k, 100k, 1m, 10m) and section 1 P4 (history depths 1, 3, 10); qualification/benchmark-contract.json (topologies, query families); acceptance review r1 finding 13. Rungs: 10000, 100000, 1000000, 10000000; every count and stratum scales proportionally with the rung; hub in-degree is 1% of the rung's entities; shares are identical at every rung. At year one: {"entities": 10000000, "activeDomainFacts": 100000000, "retainedFactsMin": 150000000, "retainedFactsNote": "TARGETS section 2: retained history 150M to 500M facts per year; the history strata below give about 162M retained facts"}. Facts per entity: 10 active domain facts: label (string), risk score (number, approximate), pay rate (decimal, scale 2), hours (integer), headcount (integer), flag (boolean), group (ref), category (string, skewed), start date (datetime), status changed at (datetime). Written through public writes (EP-WRITER, or EP-BULK for the initial load), every command ACKed with a receipt, no unresolved outcome.
  1094	
  1095	| Stratum | Rule |
  1096	| --- | --- |
  1097	| TN-LARGE | one tenant with 1m entities |
  1098	| TN-SMALL | 1,000 tenants with 1k entities each |
  1099	| TN-REST | the remaining entities in one default tenant |
  1100	| H1 | 0.5: depth 1: no correction |
  1101	| H3 | 0.35: depth 3: two corrections on each of five attributes |
  1102	| H10 | 0.15: depth 10: nine corrections on each of two attributes |
  1103	| EV-PRESENCE | 1 entity per 1,000 toggles presence true -> false -> true |
  1104	| EV-RETRO | 1% of commands are valid-time corrections 30 days back (TARGETS section 2) |
  1105	| EV-VALID-FUTURE | 5% of entities hold a fact whose validTo falls inside the measurement window |
  1106	| EV-VALID-PAST | 5% of entities hold a fact already closed by valid time |
  1107	| EV-SAME-R | 1 command per 10,000 shares its recorded instant with the next command |
  1108	| EV-DECREASING-R | 1 command per 10,000 is written by a second runtime whose clock is behind |
  1109	| EV-NESTED | 1 command per 10,000 is a nested transaction holding two positions |

