   485	
   486	Every array has a defined order (8.7). Every output is written as canonical JSON (section 9).
   487	
   488	### 8.2 Tasks
   489	
   490	- **Id:** `S + "#" + kind` for unkeyed rules; `S + "#" + kind + "#" + key` for `DOCEXP` and `PROP`. Example:
   491	  `pl:a#doc.reverify#pl:a/doc:1`. A task id does not contain the release, so one task keeps its id across releases.
   492	- **`overdue`:** `true` when `dueAt` is not `null` and `v >= dueAt`; otherwise `false`.
   493	
   494	### 8.3 Obligations
   495	
   496	**An obligation is a future valid-time instant at which this subject's output changes with no new write** (the boundary timers
   497	of R18 section 3.4 item 3). Three kinds exist:
   498	
   499	| Kind | Made by | Id | Boundary |
   500	| --- | --- | --- | --- |
   501	| `start` | `LIFE` row 2 | `S + "#start"` | `startOf(S.startDate)` |
   502	| `doc.window` | `DOCEXP` row 4 | `S + "#doc.window#" + d` | `W` |
   503	| `due` | every task with `dueAt ≠ null` and `v < dueAt` | `<task id> + "@due"` | the task's `dueAt` |
   504	
   505	A `due` obligation carries the task's rule. Every boundary is strictly greater than `v`.
   506	
   507	### 8.4 Work items (RULINGS Q36a)
   508	
   509	- **Fields:** `kind` and `key` from the rule's table (`key` is `""` for unkeyed rules, d for `DOCEXP`), `rule`, `inputs` equal to
   510	  the `inputs` of the trace entry with the same rule and key, `payload` from the table below, `id` and `version`.
   511	- **The id names the work, not its content:** `"wi:" + lowercase hex of SHA-256 over the UTF-8 bytes of
   512	  canonicalJson({"key": ..., "kind": ..., "rule": ..., "subject": S})`, with exactly those four keys. The id does not change with
   513	  the release or the inputs.
   514	- **The version names the content:** `"wv:" + lowercase hex of SHA-256 over the UTF-8 bytes of
   515	  canonicalJson({"inputs": ..., "payload": ..., "release": <release hash>})`, with exactly those three keys.
   516	- **Payloads** carry the values the rule decided on, never a PII value:
   517	
   518	| Kind | Rule | Payload |
   519	| --- | --- | --- |
   520	| `everify.submit-case` | `EVSUB` | `{"startDate": S.startDate}`, or `null` for the value when the start date is absent |
   521	| `notify.everify-tnc` | `EVSTAT` | `{"dueAt": <the everify.tnc task's dueAt, an instant or null>}` |
   522	| `notify.everify-fnc` | `EVSTAT` | `{}` |
   523	| `bgc.order` | `BGC` | `{}` |
   524	| `notify.pre-adverse-action` | `BGC` | `{}` |
   525	| `notify.document-expired` | `DOCEXP` | `{"docType": d.docType, "expiresOn": d.expiresOn}` |
   526	| `notify.pay-below-minimum` | `MINWAGE` | `{"floorCents": <the floor of 7.8>, "payRateCents": S.payRateCents}` |
   527	| `notify.pay-change-approval` | `PAYCHG` | `{"baselinePayRateCents": S.baselinePayRateCents, "payRateCents": S.payRateCents}` |
   528	
   529	- **Publication** is the outbox's rule, stated here so the expected outbox content is defined. For each work item an evaluation
   530	  produces, the outbox publishes `(id, version)` with its payload when no version of that id has been published yet, or when the
   531	  payload differs from the payload of the latest published version of that id. Otherwise it publishes nothing. The delivery key is
   532	  `(id, version)`, so a redelivered version is deduplicated at the receiver (GS.19b).
   533	- **Consequences:**
   534	  - Re-evaluating the same inputs under the same release gives the same id and the same version.
   535	  - An activation that leaves a payload unchanged publishes nothing, although the version changes with the release hash (early
   536	    cutoff, R18 X5). In C19 against C20, `bgc.order` keeps its id and its empty payload.
   537	  - An activation that changes a payload publishes a new version of the same id. In C19 against C20, `notify.pay-below-minimum`
   538	    keeps its id and its payload's floor moves from 1650 to 1700.
   539	  - W0 defines no retraction: when a work item stops appearing in the outputs, its published versions stay as they are.
   540	
